WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
Oh, my goodness.

2
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:04.260
They shot in our house.

3
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.260
We had a big picture glass window in the front.

4
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:12.500
We had all this . . . Whenever he’d be home, we would all get together because the kids were glad to see him.

5
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.140
We would have dinner.

6
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.500
We were in the dining room.

7
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.040
We got up.

8
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.040
He was leaving going to another meeting.

9
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.720
When we got up and left out of the dining room, we heard this big crash.

10
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.160
Somebody had . . . we went back in there.

11
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.753
There was a hole in the picture glass window.

12
00:00:30.753 --> 00:00:35.220
It was a bullet hole.

13
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:42.880
Of course, he went on to his meeting [laughs].

14
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.460
We called the police.

15
00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:52.660
Of course, they came on out and everything, but they never could find anything.

16
00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:53.660
Now, here’s a big bullet hole.

17
00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.960
It had ricocheted up the wall, up the glass.

18
00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.500
Oh, they couldn’t find anything.

19
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.040
They were so sorry.

20
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.180
They were going to put more protection out there.

21
00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.420
Of course, they didn’t, but nevertheless.

22
00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.900
That was one thing.

23
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:15.080
Then again, there was a cross burned on our lawn one night.

24
00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:23.880
Every weekend during the summertime . . . Have you ever tried to wash egg off of concrete when it’s ninety-something degrees?

25
00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.300
You had to scrape it up.

26
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:32.725
This is what I had to go through; sometimes during the week, but mostly on the weekends.

27
00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:37.420
Evidently they’d come down the driveway because the house was set back a little bit.

28
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.900
They would throw eggs at the front door.

29
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.000
Our front entrance would just be plastered with eggs.

30
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.320
Of course, as we say, “It was horrible.”

31
00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.880
Every time he was involved in, like when he was running for mayor,

32
00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.460
or if he had a court case coming up, or whatever, it would get worse.

33
00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.980
All of this stuff would just get worse.

34
00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:02.620
I was the one who had to get up there and scrape it up because you couldn’t wash it up.

35
00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:03.100
It wouldn’t wash up.

36
00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.900
You had to scrape it.

37
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:10.120
Then, we had as I said this cross burning.

38
00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:16.240
They sent two FBI [Federal Bureau of Investigation] agents out after all of this.

39
00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.020
When they came, they were two of the biggest men I’d ever seen in my life.

40
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:23.120
I had to look up at them.

41
00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.260
When they came out, I was . . . I had just had it.

42
00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:32.980
I don’t know where I got the courage to talk to them the way I did, but I told them.

43
00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.780
I said, “Okay, they shot in my house.

44
00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.460
They throw eggs on my house.

45
00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.880
I’m tired of scraping the egg off of my house.

46
00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.620
They’re burning a cross.”

47
00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.736
I said, “I’m telling you right now.

48
00:02:45.736 --> 00:02:51.259
My husband has bought me a gun and I am being trained to use it.”

49
00:02:51.259 --> 00:02:53.100
Which was the truth.

50
00:02:53.100 --> 00:03:00.360
I said, “I may not have to call you anymore.

51
00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:06.420
Because if I catch anybody throwing eggs at my house, I’m going to shoot.

52
00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:14.280
If I catch anybody burning a cross on my lawn, I’m going to shoot.

53
00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.360
There won’t be any point in you coming here because I will have taken care of it.”
